<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Julius Caesar</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Julius Caesar was a Roman general and statesman whose victory in civil war made him dictator, before his assassination in 44 BCE. His intervention in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/egypt">Egypt</a> supported <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cleopatra-vii">Cleopatra VII</a>, and their relationship drew the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ptolemaic-kingdom">Ptolemaic Empire</a> into Roman politics. His career paved the way for the foundation of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/roman-empire">Roman Empire</a> under Augustus.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/julius-caesar.jpg" alt="Julius Caesar" width="309" height="420" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Ángel M. Felicísimo from Mérida, España · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Retrato_de_Julio_C%C3%A9sar_(26724093101)_(cropped).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
